WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.040
My guest this week has been described

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.760
as one of the greatest English
soccer strikers of all time.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.090
As a player, Gary Lineker
scored 48 goals for England

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.720
and nearly 250 for English clubs.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.890
Since leaving the pitch,

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.640
he's become the face of football
coverage here in the UK,

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.780
and is a big vocal
presence on social media.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.700
When I sat down with him
ahead of the World Cup,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.770
I wanted to ask him about concerns

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.470
to do with Qatar's human rights record,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.680
the likes of David Beckham
doing deals with the state,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.907
and why footballers can never win.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.140
Gary, thank you so much for being here.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.532
Pleasure.
Lovely to have you.

00:00:50.532 --> 00:00:51.365
Thank you.

00:00:51.365 --> 00:00:52.680
And it's an interesting
time to talk to you

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.290
because normally for a World Cup,

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.240
there'd be a lot of the usual feelings,

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.670
excitement, trepidation.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.020
This feels quite different

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.440
because of the controversy
around where it is.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.500
Believe you me, this is the
same before every World Cup.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.620
There are different levels of
it, and this is high level,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.458
but you can go back to 1934 if you want,

00:01:15.458 --> 00:01:18.000
when the World Cup was in Italy.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.230
It was used as a vehicle to
promote fascism for Mussolini.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.660
So, this is not new.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:28.920
Brazil in 2014, there
were riots on the streets

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.050
by people in Brazil saying

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.790
they shouldn't spend all
this money on the stadiums,

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.710
they should spend it on social care.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.200
We had Russia who invaded Crimea

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.190
just a few years before
they hosted the World Cup.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:44.250
So, it is not something
we're unaccustomed to.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.810
Do you think it's on a
different scale though?

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.220
Because some of the reports, of course,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.680
about the number of
lives that have been lost

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.280
in the building of the
stadium and the preparations?

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.870
I think what makes this different

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.900
is not just in terms of human rights

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:01.680
and obviously workers' rights
and what happened to them.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.190
And lots of lives were lost
in the building of stadium.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.830
I think what is really
different about this one

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:12.450
is that we know when the bid
was proved to be successful

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.920
that it was corrupt.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.820
So I think that's what perhaps
separates this from the rest.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.230
Human rights wise,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.960
well there's a few countries
that have hosted it

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.200
that would fail some tests on that.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.820
Yeah, well let's go to that in a minute.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.840
But on the FIFA point,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.900
because the former FIFA
president, Sepp Blatter,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.970
has now said it was a mistake.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.830
He waited a long time
to do that, hasn't he?

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.194
Yeah, I mean, not in the clearest-

00:02:36.194 --> 00:02:37.027
I could have told him that

00:02:37.027 --> 00:02:39.873
the minute he opened the
thing and it said Qatar on it.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.918
I mean, do you think there's any value

00:02:42.918 --> 00:02:44.140
in that statement at this point,

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.810
or is it just pointless to hear it?

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.710
I just don't understand
why he would do that now.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.380
I dunno whether that
helps or hinders or what.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.780
I mean he's the ex president of FIFA

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.970
at a time where there was
a lot of dodgy goings on.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.670
So, yes, it was a mistake,

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.280
but it was more than a
mistake, wasn't it really?

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.190
Well, I mean also FIFA just
having put out this email,

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.810
let's not focus on the politics,

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.610
let's focus on the football.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.310
Do you think FIFA has learned as a body

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.990
about what's the important focus?

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.870
I do believe that the current...

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:19.860
Maybe I'm being naive,

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.490
but I do believe the current
people in charge of FIFA

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.160
and it includes Arsène Wenger,
he's in a really high role.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.810
I have certain amount of faith and trust

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.190
that Arsène Wenger is a decent,

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.040
upstanding, non-corrupt person.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.010
I don't think the levels of
corruption, if there are any,

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.510
there will be in certain branches of FIFA

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:40.080
'cause it's global, but
in terms of the very top,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.300
I think it's much more transparent.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.220
The voting system is much more transparent

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.510
and there's less corruption.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.160
Do they still make mistakes?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.283
Yes, they do, in terms
of things that they say.

00:03:51.644 --> 00:03:55.170
The thing you just mentioned
was very tone deaf to say that

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.700
because there's no question

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.210
that this is kind of sports washing,

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.220
but the reason sports washing works

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.310
is when you are told to shut
up about everything else

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.013
and just say, well just
stick to the football.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.490
So I think that was an error

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.650
and I think it was a tone deaf statement.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.310
And I think it's something
that most of the federations

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.630
will probably argue against.

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:21.930
Some of the players we've heard
might be wearing arm bands

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.370
in support of LGBTQ players
and people around the world.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.870
Do you think we should hear more

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.550
from the players themselves?

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.470
Well, I think it's really
interesting, isn't it?

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.290
Because the minute players stand up

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.730
and voice their concerns,

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.130
everyone tells them, "Stay outta politics.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.000
Stick to football."

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.170
Yeah.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.540
When they don't stand
up and say something,

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.310
people say, "Why aren't
you saying anything?"

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.500
So there's an element of the footballers

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:47.823
that can't win on this.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.000
They're inextricably linked,
politics and sport, all sport.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.300
There's no getting away from that fact.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.900
Politicians will use
football when it suits them.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.670
So if England start doing well

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.610
and say they get to the
quarter finals or semifinal,

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.530
we'll all have our politicians standing up

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.810
and they'll be putting England jerseys on

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.370
and pretending to be really interested.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.080
Now, some of them are
interested in football.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.250
A lot of them aren't.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.450
But even the ones that aren't

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.370
will suddenly be wanting to be seen

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:21.873
and jump on this England
bandwagon of success.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.210
But the minute footballers
voice themselves

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.970
or come out and talk about social issues,

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.740
take Marcus Rashford for example,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.650
take the captains during Covid,

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.600
all of a sudden it's like,
whoa, hang on a minute.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.550
You're getting a bit
above your station here.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.250
So footballers are allowed to speak

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.770
when it suits the
politicians, I always feel.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:47.190
It's always been a little bit
of a kind of pet hate of mine.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:48.023
Of course though,

00:05:48.023 --> 00:05:50.490
the people they answer to
are their fans, as well.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.590
So yes, the politicians
make the statements

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.060
and get the air time in response,

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.040
but I suppose it's just also,

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.320
it's been striking how
some of the female players

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:01.020
have spoken out, female
football players, about it.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.460
I was looking at the comments

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.860
from England's Lotte Wubben-Moy

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.380
who said she's not going to watch it.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.890
Beth Mead, of course, is a
hugely successful striker.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.240
She's done so well in the game.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.880
She's just winning all these
accolades. She's gay herself.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.970
She's said, "It's just so disappointing."

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.860
But it's quite a big thing to
say you're not gonna watch it

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.530
when you play football for a living.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:23.363
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:23.363 --> 00:06:25.140
But I mean, people make
their own decisions

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.943
on what they have to do.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.430
I just wondered, do you
think they're being bolder

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.350
'cause they're not involved or-

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:32.310
Of course they are, yeah.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:34.874
I mean, it's very easy to say these things

00:06:34.874 --> 00:06:37.650
if you're not gonna play in it.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:38.490
It's a different thing.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.590
Do you think footballers get
scared about speaking out

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:41.670
or get nervous?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.110
I think some will, some won't.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.790
Some are brave, some have stand out.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:45.813
I've been really proud of footballers

00:06:45.813 --> 00:06:46.920
over the last few years.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.930
I think they've really
come out on social issues.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.060
I've mentioned Rashford before.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.260
The captains during the thing.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.030
We've seen people like Raheem Sterling

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.160
speak out brilliantly on
racism and things like that.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.540
So I've been really proud of the fact

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.370
and a lot of them do
and a lot of them will.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.930
Others are less comfortable

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:04.590
and for me, it's purely a personal issue.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.300
You know, if somebody
wants to take a stand

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.670
in a certain way, that's fine.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:12.400
And if somebody just wants
to concentrate on their game

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:16.380
and possibly their only
opportunity to play in a World Cup

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:18.090
and they just wanna get on
with the football side of it

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:21.660
and not let these things
creep in, that's fine too.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.280
You've talked a bit about,

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.933
because just to say very clearly,

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.590
homosexuality is illegal in Qatar.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.120
There are also other issues

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.730
that are very different
culturally for the fans,

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:33.563
perhaps we'll come on to,

00:07:33.563 --> 00:07:35.850
but you've also talked
about it would be a moment,

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.070
not to put pressure, but it
would be a bit of a moment

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.810
if a footballer came out as gay-

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:40.643
Well, it could-
During this time.

00:07:40.643 --> 00:07:43.740
I did say that, but I didn't
say a footballer should.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:44.755
No, no, no, which is why

00:07:44.755 --> 00:07:46.230
I was making that-
The context is important.

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:47.670
So, I was saying it would be, you know,

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:51.267
a big kind of middle finger
to perhaps that thing.

00:07:51.267 --> 00:07:52.620
And it won't happen.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:53.880
I wouldn't put pressure on any player

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.173
ever to do that anyway.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.310
But of course, it's an issue,

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.690
the human rights side of things.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:01.920
It has to be.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.470
The Qatar World Cup ambassador

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.350
has just called homosexuality
damage in the mind.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:08.550
I saw that.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.640
Which is an insight into the view,

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.113
the reason for the view.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:18.900
If you were gay, as a fan,
would you go to this tournament?

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:19.950
It's a great question.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:24.950
I don't know because it's
a hypothetical question.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:28.080
You would have to give it
a lot of thought, I think.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.110
You know, I saw one of
their main representatives,

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.290
I think it was Al Thani,
speaking in an interview

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:38.613
saying that, you know, gay
people will be welcome.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.447
The question was asked,

00:08:40.447 --> 00:08:42.240
"What about if they walked
down the street holding hands?"

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.090
He said, "That would be absolutely fine."

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.556
But let's see.

00:08:46.556 --> 00:08:47.970
But there's a risk though.
But there's a risk.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:50.840
But I understand why people...

00:08:52.085 --> 00:08:55.950
If the LGBTQ, et cetera,
would have reservations

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.450
and thoughts and concerns.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.620
Absolutely.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:02.370
Whether I, you could say,
whether I would go if I were gay,

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:03.690
I honestly don't know.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:04.530
I don't know.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.690
I mean you obviously you
are going to work to-

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.880
I'm going to work, yeah. Yeah.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.068
How you feeling about that with this-

00:09:10.068 --> 00:09:11.100
No, I'm fine

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.890
but I don't have the slightest
problem about going to work.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:17.250
I'm not going there to support
the World Cup being in Qatar.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.254
I'm going there to report it.

00:09:18.254 --> 00:09:19.087
Yeah, it's a common sense.

00:09:19.087 --> 00:09:20.400
For me, that's my job

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.953
as a kind of sports
broadcaster, journalist.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:27.390
You know, journalists
will be sent to the war

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.560
with Russia and Ukraine.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.570
But it doesn't mean, say,
they support what's going on.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.860
No, no, no, and I didn't mean that,

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.750
but I meant more like if
there was any nervousness,

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.730
you know, just things like
Qatar's UK ambassadors

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.040
warned against public
displays of affection.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:38.873
I'm not saying you're gonna to be

00:09:38.873 --> 00:09:40.779
doing any affection with your colleagues.

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:42.665
Chance should be a fine thing.

00:09:42.665 --> 00:09:44.940
Happily single man, I understand.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.100
But also, for the fans,

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.020
I wonder if you've got a
nervousness about that,

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.730
not just on the human rights side,

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:51.870
but the zero tolerance

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.910
for drinking in public and being drunk.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.170
I know.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:57.300
Well, I always have concerns

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.740
about English fans traveling abroad

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:02.370
because I'm afraid a
small percentage of them

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.650
do go there looking for trouble,

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.000
looking to just get drunk,
looking for a fight.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.160
And that's been part of something,

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:14.010
it's been detestable around
the England squad for years

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.760
and they ruin it for everyone else.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.720
What will happen to them in Qatar,

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.760
I don't know if they go along that things,

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.221
but I think we've all got-

00:10:22.221 --> 00:10:23.430
Well, I think all football fans obviously

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.220
in their ranks have the
drinking side of things.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.660
Yeah, the drink, well yes.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.770
It's a nervousness perhaps
around the whole thing as well.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.650
Yeah, I'm sure. I'm sure.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:34.110
I mean, I think we'll all
be thinking ourselves, how

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.640
do we get a drink at some point.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.830
There might be that, as well.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.860
Many footballers, as
yourself, become pundits,

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:43.440
ambassadors, journalists, commentators.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:46.350
There has also been
criticism of, for instance,

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.887
David Beckham becoming a
paid ambassador to Qatar,

00:10:48.887 --> 00:10:50.850
headed to the World Cup.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.280
He's got to promote tourism
and culture in Qatar.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.750
He's become the face of it.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.760
What do you make of that sort of decision?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.490
Well that's, again, it's
a personal decision.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.170
I'm not gonna sit here and be judgemental.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.253
Would I do it? No.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:05.250
Eric Cantona, who
obviously played with him,

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.310
has spoken out and urged
him to think differently.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.710
Yeah, and I understand why he's done that.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.418
And as I said, would I have done it? No.

00:11:13.418 --> 00:11:15.900
He's decided to go down that route.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.700
I would say about David,

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.250
he's never really voiced his concerns

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:22.053
about where the World Cup is.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.610
So, you know, it's not something
he's ever got involved in.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.850
So, can you accuse him,
but he's not hypocritical.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:34.770
If I'd have done it, I was
very, very anti the bid

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.750
when it was first revealed in 2010.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:38.640
I was in the room. I couldn't believe it.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.220
It seemed to me that it
must have been corrupt

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.390
because they were talking about

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.190
staging a summer World Cup in Qatar

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:45.690
where temperatures are in the 40s,

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.900
sometimes even approaching
50 degrees centigrade.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:50.463
It seemed unfathomable.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:55.470
Then, obviously, laterally
it was moved to winter

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.660
and I was very vocal against it.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:01.230
So if I was gonna do something like that,

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:02.610
I'd feel hypocritical.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.740
I don't think you could
accuse Beckham of that.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.390
You might accuse him of doing something

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:10.800
that you might feel is
fundamentally a wrong thing to do.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.600
And a lot of people will think that.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.341
Are you disappointed by
him doing that though?

00:12:14.341 --> 00:12:16.585
'Cause he's a role model
for a lot of people.

00:12:16.585 --> 00:12:17.418
And has been.
He is a role model.

00:12:17.418 --> 00:12:20.100
As I said, I wouldn't do it.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.420
I think also people will think,

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.920
why does he need 10 million quid?

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.180
Does he really need to do that?

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.553
That's the other question
when they don't get-

00:12:25.553 --> 00:12:28.350
I mean, I have no idea how
much he's getting paid,

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.887
but I suspect-
Has he reported?

00:12:29.887 --> 00:12:32.043
I suspect he would survive without it.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:37.639
I suppose it's that, you
know, the feeling of influence

00:12:37.639 --> 00:12:39.230
and how people have influence
and what they use it for.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:44.230
Of course, you know, football is a...

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:47.447
Obviously, sport's a massive thing

00:12:47.447 --> 00:12:49.770
around the whole world anyway,
and football in particular,

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:52.290
and just before a World Cup, it is.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.930
And there's a lot of
expectancy on footballers,

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.270
but you know, there's a lot of criticism

00:12:57.270 --> 00:12:59.280
about how much they earn
and stuff like that.

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:01.650
And footballers do get it in the neck.

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.830
It's like, it's tough to win.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:07.590
Obviously they have a
wonderfully lucrative life,

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.270
but it's funny, I always think

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:13.530
they don't really get the
criticism in other people,

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:14.790
in other sports, even.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.470
Like, you know, you got lots of money,

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:18.330
like golf or Formula One

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.240
or you could even go in
other routes, like actors.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:23.610
Huge actors earn fortunes.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.070
Musicians, brilliant musicians.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.570
If you're in the entertainment industry,

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:28.830
you do get paid a lot of money,

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:31.200
but no one else gets that football,

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:35.010
it's almost as though, all
these are working class lads.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.145
It's a little bit different.

00:13:36.145 --> 00:13:36.978
Is that what you think is going on?

00:13:36.978 --> 00:13:38.610
I genuinely believe it
might be subconsciously,

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.020
but I think there's an element of that.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.790
They're a bit above their station.

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:45.120
Is it also because they can and do,

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.640
especially 'cause they're so
young earning so much money,

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.575
get into a lot of trouble at times?

00:13:49.575 --> 00:13:51.150
Like the drunk-
Well, not many of them do.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:52.830
Not many of them do.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:53.890
And the other thing is-
Is that a perception thing?

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:56.130
It is absolutely a perception thing.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.360
Footballers are a cross section

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.250
of working class society really.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:02.280
They come up and it's hard.
They have to work really hard.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:03.600
They live very well.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:06.300
Like every now and again, a
footballer will misbehave,

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:09.153
one out of, you know, there
are thousands of them around,

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.090
but that becomes a huge story.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:13.677
All the incredible good that they do

00:14:13.677 --> 00:14:16.650
for like local communities,
visiting kids in hospital,

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:18.330
doing loads of good things,

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.640
raising awareness of whether it be racism

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.530
or during the Covid pandemic,

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:24.930
that doesn't become the big story,

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:27.540
but, you know, one player goes
out in a drunken night out

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:29.730
and gets pictured with
a girl or something,

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:31.950
then that becomes like a front page story.

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:34.680
And it's a little bit unfair

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:38.250
and that doesn't really
happen as much in other areas.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.540
See, it's a disproportionate-

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:41.010
I think it's disproportionate, yeah.

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:43.080
I mean of course when actors, you know,

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:45.390
behave badly or things,
it also gets captured,

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:46.680
but it's interesting to hear

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:47.880
you think it is disproportionate.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.590
I mean, we should also say

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:52.410
there have been some
really high profile cases

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.840
and allegations made against
top class footballers

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.450
in relation to behavior with women.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:01.020
On the surface, it seems
a change in the culture

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.790
when you were playing around the game.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.378
I don't know if that's fair
and what you think around that.

00:15:05.378 --> 00:15:06.840
I don't know.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.850
I still think, when I played,

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:10.830
I doubt it's that much different now.

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:11.790
You'd have-

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.290
It's a lot more money I suppose-

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.220
Well there is a lot-

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.680
People not settling down.
There is a lot more money

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:19.080
and there'd be a lot
more, you know, dangers

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.300
and outside interests.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:23.820
I honestly think that mostly though,

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.750
like the massive majority of footballers

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.590
have been really good lads, well behaved,

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:32.040
work really, really hard on
what they do and live properly

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.740
because you have to now
because it's so competitive.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.840
And I think it was exactly
the same in my day.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:41.760
You will still get the
odd drunk, the odd sexist,

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:44.070
the odd homophobic person,

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:46.980
like a cross section of
working class society,

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:49.263
and the odd person that
will commit a crime.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.704
But it's not rife, you know.

00:15:53.704 --> 00:15:55.923
It's very occasional and limited.

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.290
I'm not trying to defend

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.301
the actions of the few.
No, no, no.

00:15:59.301 --> 00:16:00.134
I could hear that.

00:16:00.134 --> 00:16:01.565
You tried to put it in context.

00:16:01.565 --> 00:16:03.090
I'm trying to get a
context and perspective

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.160
of the overall picture of footballers.

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:07.680
I suppose though, the other
thing that's undeniable

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:11.730
is we still don't have an
openly gay male footballer

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:13.800
in the Premier League.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:17.484
What could change or how could
that change do you think,

00:16:17.484 --> 00:16:19.800
to make that a space where
it feels comfortable?

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:20.633
I don't know.

00:16:24.952 --> 00:16:26.760
I mean, it is distressing

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.520
and we're starting to see it
in other sports, aren't we,

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:31.670
you know, Tom Daley we've seen...

00:16:33.418 --> 00:16:34.251
Well in the women's game as well.

00:16:34.251 --> 00:16:36.390
In the women's game, as well.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.790
I just would love it if
we had an environment

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.320
where they just felt they should...

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.090
It seems absurd that anyone should-

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:43.034
'Cause often when you

00:16:43.034 --> 00:16:43.867
talk about society-
Be scared

00:16:43.867 --> 00:16:44.700
to say who you are.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:46.500
It can be true.
It's a society thing,

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:47.333
as well.

00:16:47.333 --> 00:16:51.750
I mean, I kind of probably naively

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.850
said something in an interview recently

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:58.110
that got picked up by quite
a few smart gay people,

00:16:58.110 --> 00:16:59.430
which I've kind of learned from.

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:01.680
I was saying, I honestly think
that if a footballer came out

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.383
it would be hugely positive
and others would follow.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.090
I was kind of told, you know,

00:17:08.361 --> 00:17:11.640
you have no idea how
difficult this situation is.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:15.720
So, I mean it's delicate and it's true.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:17.220
It's kind of baffling

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.920
because it's obvious there must be

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.840
lots of Premier League footballers

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:25.140
and footballers around
the country that are gay

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.940
and are having to live

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:31.170
and not be their true selves.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.531
And I think that's really sad.

00:17:33.531 --> 00:17:35.580
Did you, like, looking
back on your career,

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.500
do you think you played alongside men

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:40.350
who weren't their true selves in that way?

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:43.590
Oh yeah, I think so. I think so.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:48.590
I'm pretty sure. I don't know
for a fact, but I think so.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:51.355
Do you have young footballers
who come to you to say-

00:17:51.355 --> 00:17:55.710
I've had a couple, both
anonymous actually.

00:17:55.710 --> 00:18:00.603
One was very close to coming out.

00:18:02.768 --> 00:18:04.920
He was actually the secret gay footballer

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:07.920
and I was talking to him on
direct message quite a lot

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.313
and I was gonna be doing the interview,

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:14.880
but then he got cold
feet at the last second

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.410
and I said, "Well I totally respect that.

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.030
I totally understand."

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.850
And then I was reached
out through my agency,

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:24.060
another anonymous footballer
who was thinking about it.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:26.820
So I don't know who they
are, but they're out there.

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:27.960
Of course they're out there.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:28.800
And I couldn't understand

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:31.980
how incredibly difficult it must be for-

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.569
Do you think it's the fans mainly?

00:18:33.569 --> 00:18:36.090
I don't know. I don't know.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.840
It's probably everything, you know.

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:41.940
Who knows, they might not
have told their family.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:42.903
They might be scared about that.

00:18:42.903 --> 00:18:45.390
They might be scared about
telling their teammates

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:46.440
in the dressing room.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:51.540
It must be quite,
incredibly difficult. Tough.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:54.240
On your coming out with
your political views,

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.290
a different type of coming out,

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:56.960
and saying more what
you think about things,

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:00.301
it actually did take you
a long time, didn't it?

00:19:00.301 --> 00:19:01.860
It took social media.

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:02.693
Is that what it was?

00:19:02.693 --> 00:19:03.697
I mean, I've always had to, you know-

00:19:03.697 --> 00:19:04.530
No, no.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.790
I had nowhere to share them.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:09.750
And I think, you know, when
you speak out like that,

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.510
there are people who
don't like the reactions

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.730
and have ended up then self-censoring.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:15.870
Do you ever have that fear,

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:18.420
that anxiety after you've sent a post or?

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.610
I have a policy with...

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:22.230
I've got three rules in Twitter.

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:25.110
One is not to tweet when
I'm, had a few drinks,

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:26.343
which I stick to.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:31.200
The other is not to tweet if I'm angry,

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.730
but I don't really get angry.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:35.460
But, you know, when I'm too frustrated.

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:38.010
And my other one is that
whenever I do any kind of tweet,

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:43.010
I'll read it back and
then if I have 1% doubt,

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:44.550
I won't send it.
It's gone.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:47.520
Although that one, occasionally,
when I think of something

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.890
that I think actually that's quite funny,

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:51.330
I'll take a chance.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.160
But generally they are my three rules.

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:55.080
Would you pay for your authentication-

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:55.913
I wouldn't have paid-
for your blue tick?

00:19:55.913 --> 00:19:58.110
$44 billion for Twitter.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.520
That was a slightly separate deal.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.013
Well, I never asked for
it in the first place, so.

00:20:01.013 --> 00:20:03.060
No, no, but the whole idea

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:05.061
of how they're gonna
change the model, pay-

00:20:05.061 --> 00:20:07.110
Yeah, I don't know yet.
I'm gonna weigh it up.

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:09.690
I'm not gonna make any rash decision now.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.700
I mean, you know, it's not...

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.710
But the truth is actually,

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.060
I mean a lot of people are on Twitter

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:17.730
to follow people that
they find interesting,

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:18.900
mostly blue tick people,

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.180
whether they're like a politician or actor

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:25.170
or a sports person or a
musician or real comedians,

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:28.170
and you follow them and
they're the blue tick ones.

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:31.050
So actually I think it's
the blue tick people

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:33.270
that entice more people onto the platform.

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:37.290
So Elon Musk, I think should
be paying us $8 a month,

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.390
everyone on there, rather
than the other way round.

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:40.650
Well you can tweet him direct

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.137
'cause he replies it seems
to absolutely everyone.

00:20:42.137 --> 00:20:43.387
Does he? Oh, right.

00:20:43.387 --> 00:20:44.993
Especially if you've got a blue tick.

00:20:44.993 --> 00:20:46.590
I doubt he'd agree with me though.

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:48.510
I dare you to tweet him.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.570
You mentioned, of course,
the reaction to footballers,

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:54.660
former footballers like yourself,
from politicians at times

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:56.910
and you brought up the pandemic, as well.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.440
And here in the UK,

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.794
the former health secretary, Matt Hancock,

00:21:00.794 --> 00:21:03.360
when asked about footballer's
wages during the lockdown,

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.257
during the pandemic, said quote,

00:21:05.257 --> 00:21:07.650
"Everybody needs to play their
part in this national effort,

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:10.290
and that means Premier
League footballers, too."

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:13.470
He talked about taking pay
cuts. You'll remember all this.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:17.070
He's now in Australia taking
part in a reality TV show

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:19.050
called "I'm a Celebrity,
Get Me Out of Here."

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:21.150
Been suspended as a Conservative MP.

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:23.700
Do you think he's playing
his part as an MP?

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.260
I think he should have stuck

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:29.280
to telling footballers
to stick to football.

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:30.240
Yes.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:31.650
I mean, do what he wants,

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:33.420
but he's still an acting politician,

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:35.130
so it seems a bit strange to me

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:37.050
to disappear into the jungle.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:38.610
I think maybe...

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:41.340
Did you see that thing when
Rishi Sunak was welcomed

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:42.660
and he shook everyone's hand

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:44.730
and he kind of ignored
Hancock in the middle?

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:45.563
Yes.

00:21:45.563 --> 00:21:47.317
Maybe that maybe him go-
That was it.

00:21:47.317 --> 00:21:48.630
That was it. I'm going to bloody jungle.

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:50.340
It might also be the $400 grand

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:51.991
that he's been rumored to be-

00:21:51.991 --> 00:21:54.310
That might be one of the
400,000 reasons for him going.

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:55.920
We don't know.
I dunno

